From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: SM8250's PHY settings and combo mode

Valve's combo mode work programs every PHY that is not in combo mode with
SM8650's lane table and its common setting, whatever the SoC; SM8250's PHY
(1.2.1) has its own. SM8250 gets its table back and the 2-phase common
setting, and a combo table with the stock kernel's values: the PICO 4 has
two tracking cameras on CSIPHY 3, one on data lane 0 with the clock lane,
the other on data lane 2 with lane 3 as its clock.

The second endpoint's sensor links to the PHY's second sink pad, which the
driver knew only for the Frame's sensor by name.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
